1u21|n|To form or create; especially, to mold or make into a particular form; to give proper form or figure to. ; To adapt to a purpose; to regulate; to adjust; to direct; as, to shape the course of a vessel. ; To image; to conceive; to body forth. ; To design; to prepare; to plan; to arrange. ; Character or construction of a thing as determining its external appearance; outward aspect; make; figure; form; guise; as, the shape of a tree; the shape of the head; an elegant shape. ; That which has form or figure; a figure; an appearance; a being. ; A model; a pattern; a mold. ; Form of embodiment, as in words; form, as of thought or conception; concrete embodiment or example, as of some quality. ; Dress for disguise; guise. ; A rolled or hammered piece, as a bar, beam, angle iron, etc., having a cross section different from merchant bar. ; A piece which has been roughly forged nearly to the form it will receive when completely forged or fitted.	a:eus,93,3;1386,83,5;he8,78,3;1on5,76,4;hgo,75,2;cs2,64,3;emx,63,1;1ev9,52,5;4ag,50,3;jc2,49,4~k06,5,7;1wir,11,6;1ru6,3,6;1ev9,52,5;298l,35,5;ugg,13,5;1386,83,5;1lmr,25,4;6gk,26,4;1r3n,47,4	v:xbp,36,2;bu1,12,3~bu1,12,3;xbp,36,2	V:26ev,2,3~26ev,2,3	n:1c22,97,2;emx,79,3;1owg,77,3;he8,63,1;hgl,61,4;mcv,42,5;gj1,37,6;a6m,34,2;qsy,33,3;1r4p,29,2~6r5,21,8;1wa6,27,8;gj1,37,6;mcv,42,5;hgl,61,4;1gm9,4,3;1owg,77,3;qsy,33,3;emx,79,3;a6m,34,2	N:uh1,69,3;1dce,35,4~1dce,35,4;uh1,69,3
