1u2d|n|The part (usually an iron or steel plate) of a plow which cuts the ground at the bottom of a furrow; a plowshare. ; The part which opens the ground for the reception of the seed, in a machine for sowing seed.	a:p31,28,3;qw1,24,8;1st3,16,1;1593,11,6;15kq,4,5~qw1,24,8;1593,11,6;15kq,4,5;p31,28,3;1st3,16,1	V:1st3,16,1;21hb,13,5~21hb,13,5;1st3,16,1	n:1st3,26,2;1848,20,3;1cbv,17,2;1jh5,13,13;djq,5,4;3qw,5,5~1jh5,13,13;3qw,5,5;djq,5,4;1848,20,3;1st3,26,2;1cbv,17,2	N:22n,48,1;1y50,41,4;1st3,36,4;1pya,35,5;1wcr,28,7;zfo,18,9;5la,17,4;gjy,16,5;djq,15,8;11j2,7,10~11j2,7,10;zfo,18,9;htb,6,8;djq,15,8;1wcr,28,7;1pya,35,5;gjy,16,5;1y50,41,4;5la,17,4;1st3,36,4
