1ue1|a|Not able to see far; nearsighted; myopic. See Myopic, and Myopia. ; Fig.: Not able to look far into futurity; unable to understand things deep; of limited intellect. ; Having little regard for the future; heedless.	e:2753,48,3~2753,48,3
1ue6|n|imp. & p. p. of Shoot. ; of Shot ; The act of shooting; discharge of a firearm or other weapon which throws a missile. ; A missile weapon, particularly a ball or bullet; specifically, whatever is discharged as a projectile from firearms or cannon by the force of an explosive. ; Small globular masses of lead, of various sizes, -- used chiefly for killing game; as, bird shot; buckshot. ; The flight of a missile, or the distance which it is, or can be, thrown; as, the vessel was distant more than a cannon shot. ; A marksman; one who practices shooting; as, an exellent shot.	a:i3a,47,5;1st3,34,1;7md,32,8;qw1,32,4;1oc3,28,4;7c0,24,8;yjq,23,2;1oab,22,4;1t2s,22,5;1tql,21,2~7md,32,8;7c0,24,8;rwe,7,7;1t2s,22,5;i3a,47,5;1oab,22,4;1oc3,28,4;qw1,32,4;7ey,7,4;16r0,12,3	n:1st3,64,8~1st3,64,8
